.TH RFILE 1 "October 2026" "rfile 0.2.0-rc.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rfile \- identify files using a bounded Rust magic engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rfile
.RI [ options ] " FILE..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
rfile independently evaluates file magic rules and built-in text and format
recognizers. It embeds rules from file 5.48, commit
41b1123083ab0bbdfe32f6d4ec14f6aec9a91e59.
A FILE of - reads standard input. No operands prints usage and exits with status 1,
except explicit status/help/version requests.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -b , " --brief"
Omit filenames.
.TP
.BR -i , " --mime"
Print MIME type and encoding. --mime-type and --mime-encoding select either half.
.TP
.BR -k , " --keep-going"
Continue after matches. Normal output escapes embedded newlines as octal bytes.
.TP
.BI "-m " PATHS
Load source rules or v21 compiled databases. Unix lists are colon-separated.
.TP
.BI "-f " LIST
Read LF-separated filenames in option-event order. Cookie flags/database are
frozen at the first list; later formatting and limits follow their option events.
A LIST of - reads filenames from standard input outside strict sandbox mode.
.TP
.BR -L , " -h"
Follow or do not follow symbolic links. POSIXLY_CORRECT selects following by default.
.TP
.BR -z , " -Z"
Inspect compiled codecs with finite nested decoding budgets. -Z hides the outer
description. Default builds include gzip/zlib; extended-codecs enables additional
selected formats. Uncompiled/unsupported codecs return explicit errors.
.TP
.BR -r , " -0 , " -N , " -n"
Print raw bytes; add NUL after filename; omit padding; flush each record.
Repeating -0 also NUL-terminates the result and removes the separator.
.TP
.BI "-F " SEP
Use SEP instead of the filename colon.
.TP
.BR -E , " -s , " -p"
Report filesystem failures as errors; permit device reads; restore access times.
.TP
.BI "-e " TEST
Exclude a detector. See --help for names. --exclude-quiet ignores unknown names.
.TP
.BI "-P " NAME=VALUE
Set a resource parameter. Additional Rust budgets are steps, work and output.
.TP
.BR --extension , " --apple"
Print extension or Apple annotations.
.TP
.BR -C , " -c , " -l"
Compile, check or list rules. Use -m to select the source/database.
Check/list output and partial-load behavior follow the pinned profile for the
tested source cases. Broader warnings, DEBUG and IO/discovery behavior retain
documented compatibility boundaries.
.TP
.B --profile=pinned-5.48|corrected-v1
Select pinned file 5.48 behavior (the default), or the explicitly implemented
corrections. Corrected mode does not imply that every planned correction exists.
.TP
.B --capabilities
Print JSON describing compiled features, current profiles and qualification
status. Optional features and completed security gates must not be inferred
from the version number.
.TP
.BR --sandbox=auto|strict|off , " -S"
Select optional Linux CLI confinement; -S means off. Last selection wins.
With the sandbox feature on x86_64 Linux/glibc, auto is the default and attempts
Landlock/seccomp read-only restrictions before resource parsing. Auto is not
input-confined. Strict requires seccomp and Landlock ABI 5 or later; classification
preopens at most 128 input entries, then denies new content opens. Strict rejects
stdin filename lists and no-buffer file lists. Stdin content is supported.
Compilation has a separate output-directory write policy; mixed compile and
classification plans are rejected while sandboxing is enabled. Check/list retain
read-only filesystem scope. Library classification does not install restrictions.
.TP
.B --sandbox-status
Print actual enforcement and read scope as JSON on stderr. This does not alter
ordinary classification stdout. Unsupported builds report compiled=false; strict
fails. Kernel feature absence may degrade auto with a warning; installation
errors fail. Nonempty LD_PRELOAD is rejected in strict mode.
.TP
.BR -v , " --version , " --help"
Display version/build features or help. Version does not attest runtime confinement.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
MAGIC supplies a database list when -m is absent. HOME supplies optional .magic
configuration before the embedded default. POSIXLY_CORRECT enables symlink following.
LC_ALL, LC_CTYPE and LANG select immutable display contexts. C is portable;
selected UTF-8 locales use the Linux/glibc adapter. TZ selects an immutable
timezone context. No process-global locale/environment mutation is performed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means classification completed, including unknown data and ordinary per-file
filesystem diagnostics. -E, setup failures, resource errors and failed writes
produce status 1. A classification is a heuristic, not validation of the whole file.
.SH FILES
The default rules are embedded; normal operation needs neither libmagic nor a C
compiler. See data/UPSTREAM.json and data/SOURCES.json for data provenance.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Version 0.2.0-rc.1 is experimental. The downloadable CLI targets x86_64 Linux/glibc
with default gzip/zlib inspection. CDF/ELF enrichment, immutable local-time and
locale handling, and bounded regex captures are implemented with documented
compatibility boundaries. Additional codecs, Linux confinement and a distinct
librfile_magic C interface are experimental source-build options and are omitted
from that CLI archive. Native regex-history fidelity, broader diagnostics and
other platform coverage remain incomplete. See docs/06-implementation-status.md
and docs/release-scope.md for exact scope. Sustained fuzzing and independent
security qualification remain open; this is not a certified libmagic replacement.
